          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the mixer for the batch you need, not the drum on the box. For most homeowners that means the Kushlan 600DD for slabs and steps, the Kushlan 350DD for posts and small footings, or the Yardmax YM0146 if you prefer a tilting drum that pours into a wheelbarrow. Plan on roughly half the drum volume per load, and size the job in 80 lb bags before you start.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For thinset, grout and mortar, skip the drum and buy a proper paddle mixer, such as the DeWalt DCD130 or Collomix Xo 1 R. For anything under five bags, a wheelbarrow and hoe is quicker. For anything over a yard, call a ready-mix supplier. If you are equipping a whole yard project, our roundup of the <a href="/best-garden-tools/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">best garden tools</a> covers the other hand tools worth owning.
